+# Independent presentation telemetry, version 1
+
+This local extension exports `OptiScaler_GetPresentationStatsV1(out, bytes)`.
+Its 96-byte, pack-8 C ABI is defined in
+`OptiScaler/framegen/PresentationStats.h`. Call from the immediate render/present
+thread, outside an existing OptiScaler presentation-mutex critical section.
+Return 1 means a visible-chain snapshot was obtained; check the individual
+validity flags and HRESULTs before using either DXGI counter. Return 0 means
+unavailable, -1 invalid output arguments, and -2 a caught exception.
+
+No Streamline state counter is read or reset. The API unwraps the official
+Streamline native-interface IID, verifies a D3D12 device and the same-process
+visible game HWND, and queries that output swapchain. It never queries
+`State.currentRealSwapchain`: that is the hidden D3D11 bridge swapchain here.
+All COM references are released before the call returns.
+
+`clientPresents` counts successful, non-TEST calls at the outer FG swapchain.
+`nativePresentCalls` accumulates native DXGI `GetLastPresentCount` deltas.
+`displayedFrames` is the fixed ABI field name for accumulated DXGI
+`GetFrameStatistics().PresentCount` deltas. That field is **not a count of panel
+scanouts or proof of unique visible frames**. It should be labelled
+`DXGIstatsCounter` in diagnostics. Present-call throughput, reported display
+statistics, and the requested multiplier are separate measurements.
+
+The totals remain monotonic for the DLL lifetime and querying never clears them.
+Compare deltas only when the epoch matches, both relevant validity flags are
+set, and neither endpoint indicates a new baseline. Identity/window/size/format,
+observed FG mode or requested multiplier changes, successful swapchain resizes,
+release, and detected counter discontinuities invalidate the baseline.
+Ordinary uint32 counter rollover is supported. `requestedMultiplier` is
+configuration metadata, not a measured multiplier.
+
+For a stable 5-second interval after warm-up, report:
+
+* `delta(nativePresentCalls) / delta(clientPresents)` as native presentation-call
+  amplification, alongside both integer deltas.
+* `delta(nativePresentCalls) / elapsedQpcSeconds` as native present-call rate.
+* The independent DXGI statistics raw values, validity/HRESULT, and
+  `lastDisplayQpc`. Do not manufacture a rate when the statistics are unsupported
+  or disjoint. No blocking DwmFlush is issued to force their availability.
+
+Check a 1x baseline and then requested 2x, 3x, and 4x separately. Generated-frame
+pacing is asynchronous, so boundary effects can shift a short window by a few
+frames. Corroborate with ETW/PresentMon when claiming observed output throughput.
+Window occlusion, focus, refresh-rate limits and compositor drops can affect
+display results; API calls alone do not prove what the panel scanned out.
+
+Primary API documentation:
+
+* https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/dxgi/nf-dxgi-idxgiswapchain-getlastpresentcount
+* https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/dxgi/nf-dxgi-idxgiswapchain-getframestatistics
+* https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/dxgi/ns-dxgi-dxgi_frame_statistics
+* https://github.com/NVIDIA-RTX/Streamline/blob/main/docs/ProgrammingGuide.md#53-detecting-sl-proxies
+
+The original late-HUDless ABI1 is unchanged. Build this variant with
+`Build-Local.ps1 -BuildDirectoryName local-build-presentation`; it does not replace
+the prior local build, the stage, or the installed game backend.
